# TwichUI rules (World of Warcraft: Forever addon, Lua)

## Project
TwichUI is a focused, curated interface companion for WoW: Forever. It is not a UI replacement or a bundle of unrelated utilities.
Feature test: does it make the game clearer, more personal or more enjoyable without taking attention from the world or control from the player?
No intrusive prompts, chat spam, persistent reminders or hand-holding. Never automate protected gameplay actions.
Use the project's own spelling and namespace. Do not rename TwichUI.

## Layout (use this instead of searching)
Repo root: /home/rich/dev/personal/TwichUI/
- `!!!TwichUI/` is the addon folder. Spelled T-w-i-c-h-U-I. There is NO "t" after "Twi". Never write "TwitchUI".
- `!!!TwichUI/` holds feature modules
- `TwichUI_Settings/pages/` holds settings pages (separate load-on-demand addon)

## Paths
- Copy file paths exactly from tool output or from my message. Never retype or "correct" a path.
- Use the read tool with workspace-relative paths (e.g. `!!!TwichUI/modules/FoodDrink.lua`), not `cat` with absolute paths.
- If a file read fails, stop and show me the exact error. Do not write code for a file you have not read.
- `grep` exit code 1 means no matches, not an error.
## Hard rules
1. Target is WoW: Forever, not Retail or Classic. Before using an API you are not certain exists in this client, search the Blizzard source reference for its name. If you cannot find it, say so and ask. Never invent an API.
2. Lua syntax supported by the WoW client only: no `goto`, no `//`, no bitwise operators.
3. Use `local` everywhere. Use the addon namespace. No new globals.
4. Never edit `Libs/`, reference addons or the Blizzard source. Edit only this repository, never the deployed AddOns copy.
5. Never rename SavedVariables or change existing keys. Apply defaults only to missing values. Keep valid `false`, `0` and `""`.
6. Never use `loadstring` or `load`. Treat imports and addon messages as untrusted: validate size, version, types and structure.
7. Respect combat lockdown (`InCombatLockdown()`). Do not bypass protected or secure UI restrictions.
8. Settings live in the TwichUI-owned settings window, not Blizzard's AddOns panel. Open it through the central open/navigate function. Core features must work without the settings window ever opening.
9. Do not add libraries, dependencies or copied code without asking.
10. Do not commit, deploy, publish, or change `.toc` interface/version numbers unless asked.
11. Prefer events over `OnUpdate`. No duplicate hooks, frames, timers or callbacks. Keep caches and queues bounded.
12. Visuals: warm charcoal, umber, aged bronze, muted gold, parchment and ivory text. No neon, glass effects, heavy gradients or heavy glow. Reuse the shared styling helpers. Windows must look complete without EllesmereUI installed.
13. Make the smallest change that solves the request. No unrelated cleanup, renaming or reformatting.

## How to work
1. Read only the files you need. Check the layout above first. Do not re-search for a file you already found; remember its path.
2. Before editing, state in 2 to 3 lines which files you will change and why.
3. If the task needs more than about 3 files, touches architecture, or is ambiguous, stop and propose a plan first. For research or planning requests, change no files.
4. If you are stuck or repeating yourself, stop and ask me one specific question instead of looping.
5. Run lint or tests only if the command is listed here. Do not invent commands: `[FILL IN or delete this line]`.
6. When finished, report: files changed, what and why, checks you actually ran, what I must test in game (`/reload`, what to look for), and any risk. Never say something was tested if you did not run it.

## Deeper guidance
For work on the settings window, config sharing and backups, Journey Chronicle, shared pins or location, optional skins, or mage/inventory/trade features, search `CLAUDE.md` for that feature's heading and read only that section. Do not read the whole file.
